WEBVTT

00:03.000 --> 00:09.030
Once upon a time, when Trapla
 was still divided into four lands,

00:10.650 --> 00:17.070
evil soldiers from beyond the sea 
came to conquer the island.

00:18.700 --> 00:25.410
They stole food and preyed on the people,
leaving our peaceful island in ruins.

00:26.100 --> 00:33.940
But then, a mage appeared alongside 
 a young boy with a message...

00:34.390 --> 00:38.090
"This boy is the true king of Trapla.

00:38.490 --> 00:44.040
If you wish to save the island, choose 
thirteen knights from each of the four lands

00:44.040 --> 00:45.690
and fight by his side."

00:46.620 --> 00:52.620
In the end, an army of 52 knights was formed
 from the four lands to save the island,

00:53.270 --> 00:57.100
and the mage gifted each of them
 a mysterious card.

00:57.410 --> 01:02.950
As a token of their fealty to the boy, 
the knights swore a blood oath.

01:05.460 --> 01:11.210
They fought with all their might 
for the island and their families,

01:12.120 --> 01:17.470
yet every one perished on the battlefield, 
unable to fulfill their mission.

01:18.530 --> 01:22.250
But that did not stop 
their purpose from living on.

01:22.250 --> 01:29.480
Their love for the land was transferred
 to their cards via the mage's power.

01:30.440 --> 01:34.590
Thus the boy gained mysterious 
powers from all 52 cards,

01:35.150 --> 01:39.780
and went on to defeat the evil soldiers 
and protect the island.

01:40.860 --> 01:47.650
That was how he united the four lands 
and became the first king of Fourland.

01:50.500 --> 01:58.420
This famous legend, "The King and 
the 52 Knights," is not just a fairy tale.

01:58.880 --> 02:04.390
It is historical fact that Trapla Island 
faced the grave danger of invasion.

02:05.390 --> 02:10.440
The 52 cards created as symbols 
of the king's reign over the four lands

02:10.440 --> 02:13.150
are also real!

02:16.150 --> 02:21.400
And one such traditional masterpiece 
that has watched over the history of Fourland

02:21.400 --> 02:27.410
will grace us aboard this luxury 
cruise ship, the <i>Queen Black Lady</i>!

02:29.290 --> 02:34.220
Now, let us raise the curtain on
 this exquisite dinner party and auction

02:34.220 --> 02:38.600
for all you sophisticated
 ladies and gentlemen!

04:18.140 --> 04:22.360
<i>Dear guests, we hope you're enjoying your 
time aboard our dinner cruise ship.</i>

04:22.810 --> 04:25.490
<i>Next up, we'll interview Norman Kingstat,</i>

04:25.490 --> 04:30.120
<i>the CEO of the up-and-coming 
car manufacturer Who's Who.</i>

04:31.580 --> 04:32.680
<i>Hello, Norman.</i>

04:32.680 --> 04:33.580
<i>It's "King."</i>

04:33.580 --> 04:34.460
<i>Huh?</i>

04:34.460 --> 04:40.500
<i>I'd like for you to call me King.
So please address me as such, hmm?</i>

04:41.010 --> 04:44.030
<i>Er, certainly... K-King it is, then.</i>

04:44.340 --> 04:48.410
<i>S-So, King, what inspired you
 to attend today's auction—</i>

04:48.410 --> 04:51.600
<i>Do you think I could have resisted,</i>

04:51.600 --> 04:54.410
<i>knowing that a treasure of 
Fourland would be on display?!</i>

04:54.410 --> 04:56.600
<i>Um, well...</i>

04:56.600 --> 04:58.280
<i>The answer is no!</i>

04:58.280 --> 04:59.610
<i>Absolutely not!</i>

05:00.080 --> 05:04.860
<i>There is no one else who loves 
and is loved by this country like me!</i>

05:06.280 --> 05:08.120
<i>I-I see.</i>

05:08.530 --> 05:11.670
<i>We expect a fierce competition 
over the featured treasure.</i>

05:11.670 --> 05:13.010
<i>How confident are you—</i>

05:13.010 --> 05:16.010
<i>What a ridiculous question!</i>

05:16.010 --> 05:17.880
<i>You shall see!</i>

05:17.880 --> 05:21.770
<i>That card 100 percent belongs to me, King!</i>

05:27.030 --> 05:29.650
So this guy's after the card too?

05:31.250 --> 05:33.320
Yup, he is.

05:34.410 --> 05:35.530
How come?

05:35.530 --> 05:36.490
Beats me.

05:36.490 --> 05:38.400
You don't know?

05:38.400 --> 05:43.900
It might have something to do with the fact 
that he sees our president as an enemy.

05:44.250 --> 05:46.020
The whole lot of them are tricky.

05:46.020 --> 05:52.410
Especially Norman's secretaries, 
Blist Blitz Broadhurst and Brandy Blumenthal.

05:52.920 --> 05:56.190
These two are players, 
so we need to be cautious...

05:57.180 --> 05:58.430
Hey, are you listening?

05:58.430 --> 05:59.620
I am.

05:59.620 --> 06:00.990
Are you okay?

06:00.990 --> 06:02.070
For today's mission,

06:02.070 --> 06:07.550
we're supposed to outwit everybody on board 
and swap the real card with this fake.

06:10.150 --> 06:12.830
Who would've thought you'd get seasick?

06:12.830 --> 06:14.310
Shut up...

06:14.310 --> 06:16.140
Whoa there!

06:14.940 --> 06:16.840
Hey! Knock it off!

06:16.840 --> 06:18.290
Here you are, Finn.

06:18.290 --> 06:19.450
Thanks.

06:20.910 --> 06:24.940
Anyway, this mission 
is essentially a heist, right?

06:24.940 --> 06:26.320
And that's all fine and dandy?

06:26.320 --> 06:27.380
It's fine.

06:28.050 --> 06:31.820
The Pinochles have secretly protected 
the cards throughout Fourland's history.

06:32.590 --> 06:34.580
All without putting ourselves
 in the spotlight.

06:34.580 --> 06:39.580
Besides, fighting for it in an auction with
 no bidding limit wouldn't be ideal.

06:40.070 --> 06:42.540
The cards belong to the royal family.

06:42.540 --> 06:44.630
We're just returning them
 to their rightful owner.

06:46.040 --> 06:49.750
In other words, there's nothing wrong 
with what we're doing in principle.

06:49.750 --> 06:54.760
Before you joined us, the card being 
auctioned today was already secured,

06:54.760 --> 06:56.960
and housed at Trapla Palace.

06:56.960 --> 06:58.830
Yeah, I heard.

06:58.830 --> 07:01.570
But the Klondikes raided the palace,

07:01.570 --> 07:05.310
and the cards were scattered 
all over Fourland. Just like that.

07:06.220 --> 07:12.670
We're still investigating how
 they ended up like that, but...

07:13.640 --> 07:15.530
You don't look too well.

07:15.530 --> 07:17.820
It's nothing, really—

07:19.380 --> 07:21.720
Looks like we'll have to change the plan.

07:21.720 --> 07:23.100
Hold on!

07:23.100 --> 07:24.460
I can do this!

07:24.710 --> 07:29.240
This mission requires bold 
yet delicate execution.

07:29.720 --> 07:31.560
The smallest blunder could ruin it all.

07:31.560 --> 07:34.720
In the worst-case scenario, 
we'll all wind up with criminal charges.

07:34.950 --> 07:38.860
We can't have your vomitus 
soiling Pinochle's reputation—

07:39.820 --> 07:42.380
C'mon, Finn says he can do it.

07:42.380 --> 07:43.610
Why don't we trust him?

07:43.610 --> 07:45.480
You want me to trust <i>this guy</i>?

07:45.480 --> 07:49.290
A capable boss should be able to manage 
even the most troublesome subordinate,

07:49.290 --> 07:51.160
don't you agree?

07:52.850 --> 07:53.990
Fine.

07:55.780 --> 08:00.470
And if worse comes to worst, 
I'll take responsibility as his mentor.

08:00.470 --> 08:04.000
Boil me! Burn me! Hang me! Filet me!
 Whatever you'd like!

08:04.380 --> 08:06.130
But you're immortal.

08:13.130 --> 08:14.850
Very well.

08:16.390 --> 08:18.740
We will now begin the mission.

08:19.940 --> 08:21.320
Fifteen thousand!

08:21.320 --> 08:22.300
Twenty!

08:22.300 --> 08:23.570
Twenty-three thousand!

08:23.980 --> 08:25.670
We're at twenty-three thousand.

08:25.670 --> 08:30.020
The item is lot number 20, a ceremonial
 sword owned by a knight of Spada.

08:30.020 --> 08:31.660
Do I hear any other bids?

08:31.660 --> 08:33.170
Twenty-four thousand!

08:33.170 --> 08:34.570
Twenty-six thousand!

08:34.570 --> 08:38.330
I hope you don't mind me taking the card.

08:36.860 --> 08:38.330
Twenty-nine thousand!

08:39.030 --> 08:39.970
Suit yourself.

08:39.970 --> 08:40.830
Thirty-three thousand!

08:41.110 --> 08:42.970
We're at 33,000!

08:42.970 --> 08:44.460
Any other takers?

08:44.460 --> 08:45.460
Fifty thousand.

08:46.340 --> 08:47.150
Fifty thousand!

08:47.150 --> 08:48.750
We have 50,000!

08:48.750 --> 08:51.870
Do I hear any other bids?

08:50.890 --> 08:52.710
This is just a warmup.

08:51.870 --> 08:52.710
Anyone?

08:52.940 --> 08:57.150
Lot 20 is sold! 
To the gentleman with number one!

08:58.450 --> 09:00.520
Let's go over the plan one more time.

09:01.880 --> 09:02.870
Finn's up first.

09:03.210 --> 09:05.230
You'll steal the key from the supervisor.

09:07.350 --> 09:11.450
Hurry up. We need to prepare 
lots 23 and 24 simultaneously.

09:11.450 --> 09:13.740
Do you read me, transport team?

09:17.290 --> 09:18.460
Hey, what gives?

09:18.460 --> 09:20.730
I'm sorry... I got seasick.

09:20.730 --> 09:23.000
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry...

09:37.130 --> 09:38.750
May I take this?

09:38.750 --> 09:39.640
Certainly.

09:58.490 --> 10:00.120
Next up is Wendy.

10:00.120 --> 10:03.790
She'll get security into a cabin
 with a staged accident.

10:09.930 --> 10:11.290
I'm so sorry!

10:11.290 --> 10:13.050
Oh, don't worry about it.

10:13.050 --> 10:15.830
Are you hurt, miss?

10:19.180 --> 10:21.030
I really am sorry.

10:21.030 --> 10:23.250
Please use the shower in my cabin.

10:23.250 --> 10:26.850
There's no way you can 
go back to work like this.

10:27.180 --> 10:28.380
B-But...

10:28.380 --> 10:30.750
I can't just turn a blind eye.

10:30.750 --> 10:32.980
N-No, thank you—

10:30.990 --> 10:32.280
Please, do come in.

10:42.750 --> 10:44.190
<i>Vijay is up next.</i>

10:44.510 --> 10:47.690
<i>Your "Green Green" will come in handy.</i>

11:02.090 --> 11:03.850
Hey, are you done yet?

11:04.140 --> 11:05.250
<i>Not yet.</i>

11:05.250 --> 11:07.450
<i>I need you to buy me some more time.</i>

11:07.450 --> 11:08.440
<i>Much obliged.</i>

11:08.860 --> 11:10.770
Wait... Seriously?!

11:12.110 --> 11:13.860
Thank you very much!

11:14.930 --> 11:16.750
Is something the matter?

11:18.590 --> 11:20.510
Would you like a drink?

11:20.850 --> 11:23.870
While we wait for your clothes to dry, I mean.

11:23.870 --> 11:26.090
No, I couldn't possibly—

11:26.090 --> 11:27.870
O-Oh, don't be shy!

11:28.180 --> 11:29.670
So, how about it?

11:30.500 --> 11:34.000
Well, I really shouldn't—

11:34.000 --> 11:36.750
<i>I've obtained the security card.</i>

11:37.170 --> 11:37.910
Good.

11:37.910 --> 11:39.010
You're up last, Chris.

11:40.100 --> 11:43.100
Grab the 5 of diamonds from the vault.

11:45.160 --> 11:47.550
Now show me your security card.

11:49.220 --> 11:50.340
What's the matter?

11:50.340 --> 11:51.520
Where's your card?

11:56.870 --> 12:00.220
Psych! Did I fool you?

12:00.220 --> 12:02.120
Stop messing around and get moving already!

12:02.120 --> 12:03.480
Okay.

13:18.590 --> 13:20.190
Now, everyone!

13:20.190 --> 13:24.760
This next item is the last of our collection
of artifacts from the folklore of Fourland.

13:24.760 --> 13:26.280
It's our grand finale!

13:27.180 --> 13:33.410
A prestigious treasure should be handled 
with all the brilliant grace it deserves.

13:33.410 --> 13:39.590
And that is why <i>I</i> shall
 win this bid, fair and square!

13:42.170 --> 13:43.300
What's the status?

13:43.770 --> 13:45.170
Not too bad.

13:48.180 --> 13:49.680
You're doing it again.

13:51.950 --> 13:55.810
Sitting idly by is harder than I expected.

13:57.690 --> 13:59.690
Excuse me, King.

14:03.350 --> 14:07.320
I realize this is a sudden request, 
but why don't we take a little break here?

14:07.320 --> 14:11.460
What? But we're about 
to unveil the legendary card—

14:10.210 --> 14:12.100
Why don't you just zip it?

14:12.100 --> 14:15.290
King requires a bathroom break.

14:17.590 --> 14:19.970
I guess he couldn't hold it in.

14:47.910 --> 14:50.540
Now you've done it, Blist!

14:52.070 --> 14:55.120
Switching the genuine article with a fake?

14:55.120 --> 14:56.940
What a cheap trick.

15:00.120 --> 15:03.830
What's happening with 
the sneaky thieving rats?

15:03.830 --> 15:06.440
Blist will dispose of them momentarily.

15:06.750 --> 15:08.340
Very good!

15:08.340 --> 15:12.200
I'll take them on
 straight-up, head-on, all-out.

15:12.200 --> 15:16.260
Our skills and expertise
 will make those brats cry!

15:19.020 --> 15:22.090
Everyone, please calm down and stay seated!

15:22.090 --> 15:23.260
What's going on?

15:34.990 --> 15:38.910
Your "Million Volt" is pretty electrifying.

15:46.510 --> 15:48.130
Hey, what's going on?!

15:48.510 --> 15:49.590
Answer me!

15:49.960 --> 15:51.510
Chris, what's the situation?!

15:52.740 --> 15:55.260
Wendy, Finn! What's happening?!

15:55.670 --> 15:56.660
<i>Wendy!</i>

15:56.660 --> 15:59.270
It's dark in here!

16:00.600 --> 16:02.790
<i>Th-This is Finn...</i>

16:02.790 --> 16:05.020
<i>I'll go check out what's happening.</i>

16:05.020 --> 16:05.520
Finn!

16:05.520 --> 16:07.450
<i>Are you sure you're okay?</i>

16:07.450 --> 16:08.550
Probably...

16:10.940 --> 16:12.930
Oh, <i>do</i> calm down!

16:13.740 --> 16:15.530
Thank you for waiting, everyone.

16:15.530 --> 16:18.540
Let's resume the auction, shall we?

16:18.540 --> 16:25.660
P-Pardon, but because of the situation, 
the final item has not yet arrived—

16:23.910 --> 16:25.660
No problem!

16:25.660 --> 16:30.410
My eyes can clearly see
 the brilliant X-Playing...

16:30.410 --> 16:34.040
I mean, extremely brilliant card!

16:34.420 --> 16:36.550
I'm starting the bid at 500 thousand!

16:36.550 --> 16:41.850
Is there anyone here 
with the backbone to outbid me?

16:41.850 --> 16:43.890
If so, come forward! Come! Come now!

16:43.890 --> 16:45.600
Excuse me, sir—

16:45.600 --> 16:46.680
Six hundred thousand.

16:47.930 --> 16:51.410
L-Leo, we shouldn't do anything 
reckless until we know more.

16:52.090 --> 16:54.990
A cheap provocation, 
as expected from Who's Who.

16:55.340 --> 16:56.740
This one is going to cost you!

17:09.740 --> 17:11.040
Give up.

17:11.040 --> 17:14.680
This card will be transported 
to the auction hall as scheduled.

17:15.830 --> 17:18.030
That's what King wishes.

17:18.590 --> 17:21.260
We're definitely taking that card.

17:22.040 --> 17:25.690
Yeah, as members of High Card!

17:27.270 --> 17:29.520
Finn?! What are you doing here?!

17:29.970 --> 17:32.510
I came to help you, of course.

17:32.870 --> 17:35.330
Now get away from Chris—

17:38.170 --> 17:39.990
Pinochle's rookie, huh?

17:39.990 --> 17:41.910
You don't look so good.

17:42.220 --> 17:44.910
Now, we're through playing cops and robbers!

17:46.660 --> 17:48.170
I bid 1.5 million.

17:48.170 --> 17:49.400
I bid 1.6 million.

17:49.400 --> 17:50.820
I bid 1.8 million!

17:50.820 --> 17:51.920
I bid 1.85 million!

17:51.920 --> 17:53.540
I bid 1.9 million!

17:52.420 --> 17:55.490
Leo, let's stay calm. Leo!

17:53.540 --> 17:56.770
Two million... No, 2.1 million!

18:03.220 --> 18:05.890
In that case, I bid 2.4 million!

18:06.390 --> 18:07.640
Three million!

18:07.640 --> 18:09.370
Th-Three million?!

18:09.370 --> 18:11.250
We have three million!

18:11.730 --> 18:13.850
Well, look at you.

18:14.150 --> 18:17.400
"Losing" isn't part 
of the Pinochle vocabulary!

18:19.460 --> 18:21.660
Come on. Hurry it up.

18:30.420 --> 18:33.490
Okay, Blist. I lose.

18:33.490 --> 18:35.010
Don't do it, Chris—

18:35.800 --> 18:40.050
However, our boss isn't gonna
 lose to your "King"...

18:40.050 --> 18:42.100
and that's a fact!

18:45.350 --> 18:47.060
Hold up!

18:53.390 --> 18:55.370
Ten million!

19:01.650 --> 19:02.850
But wait!

19:02.850 --> 19:06.350
As if in response to King's summon, 
today's final item has arrived at last.

19:06.350 --> 19:11.100
Behold one of the legendary cards
spoken of in the mythos of Fourland!

19:11.100 --> 19:14.130
The bid now stands at ten million!

19:14.130 --> 19:16.680
Do I hear any other takers?

19:14.130 --> 19:16.680
M-Me! I'll—

19:22.790 --> 19:24.890
Sold for ten million!

19:25.110 --> 19:28.270
The legendary artifact goes to...

19:29.850 --> 19:34.150
Tonight's card belongs to me, King!

19:36.630 --> 19:42.100
As they say... money is power!

19:43.350 --> 19:44.250
Hmm?

19:49.000 --> 19:50.290
What?!

19:57.100 --> 19:58.530
<i>Power</i> is power.

19:58.530 --> 20:00.680
The strong prevail.

20:00.680 --> 20:02.680
That's how this world works.

20:11.180 --> 20:12.670
What the...

20:14.230 --> 20:21.820
What the hell was that?!

20:22.900 --> 20:27.180
<i>This is a follow-up report on the incident 
aboard the luxury liner </i>Queen Black Lady<i>.</i>

20:27.490 --> 20:30.490
<i>Regarding the auction being held on the ship,</i>

20:30.490 --> 20:35.580
<i>we interviewed the CEO of Who's Who, 
Mr. Norman Kingstat, who was in attendance.</i>

20:33.140 --> 20:35.060
I wish they'd let this go.

20:35.060 --> 20:36.580
Everyone's talking about it.

20:35.580 --> 20:39.210
<i>We also revealed some 
of his suspicious conduct...</i>

20:37.110 --> 20:39.900
I never expected <i>them</i> to take such 
a daring, unabashed measure.

20:39.900 --> 20:41.710
That was a lack of foresight on my part.

20:41.710 --> 20:44.510
Do you mean Norman, or...

20:44.510 --> 20:47.220
Or could you mean the real culprit was...

20:47.540 --> 20:50.090
Nine outta ten, it was the Klondikes.

20:50.090 --> 20:52.170
They can be so pushy, you know?

20:52.170 --> 20:53.700
This is no laughing matter.

20:53.700 --> 20:55.480
The card was stolen.

20:56.460 --> 20:57.640
My bad!

20:57.640 --> 21:01.100
Just who do you think is responsible
 for the failure of this mission?

21:01.820 --> 21:05.260
Was that heated bidding war part of the plan?

21:11.030 --> 21:17.510
Ban! How dare he ruin my elegant 
victory in such a vile manner?!

21:17.510 --> 21:21.190
But the fact remains 
that I outbid that Pinochle brat!

21:21.190 --> 21:25.470
So how come no one is talking about it?!
There's no mention of it anywhere!

21:25.470 --> 21:29.470
Blist! Get me an exclusive interview!

21:29.470 --> 21:34.340
Tell the press to do an in-depth 
report on King's victory!

21:34.920 --> 21:37.350
Wait, where did Blist go?

21:37.730 --> 21:40.150
He's on a paid leave today.

21:40.150 --> 21:41.480
Paid leave?

21:41.810 --> 21:45.390
Oh, as I recall, today is
 parents' day at his kid's school.

21:45.390 --> 21:50.490
Even King cannot take away 
the rights granted to his workers.

21:50.860 --> 21:54.210
Now, I can't afford to dwell on the past.

21:54.620 --> 22:01.570
Next time, I will meet the enemy 
head-on and beat him thoroughly!

23:36.200 --> 23:39.160
Next time: "LOVE & FAKE."
